+# Advanced runbook: Scale generative serving with Triton / vLLM and Warm-Pool
+
+1) Capacity planning:
+ - Map model sizes to GPU memory usage; reserve 10-20% headroom per node.
+ - Use nodePool taints/tolerations to isolate generative workloads.
+
+2) Warm pool & batching:
+ - Deploy warm-pool processes co-located with heavy models.
